contentText:
Olivia Rodrigo kicked off her inaugural Daisy Chain Fields festival with an all-female lineup including Chappell Roan, Doechii, Rachel Chinouriri, Eli, Mitski and more. Rodrigo also included special guests like Sarah McLachlan, Alanis Morissette and Stevie Nicks. In a press conference, Rodrigo talked about how ticket sales from the Daisy Chain Fields festival are going to support 10 organizations.

Olivia Rodrigo&nbsp;

You guys, this is the best day in my f&#8212;ing life. We are donating $10 million to be given directly to these 10 nonprofit partners. When I had the idea for this festival, I called each of them, and I was so overwhelmed by their enthusiasm for the idea.

Rachel Chinouriri

I got a phone call from Olivia. It was quite mad because I was just in my flat in London, and when your manager says, &#8220;Would it be OK if I give Olivia Rodrigo your number?&#8221; It&#8217;s not something you really expect. So I was just like, &#8220;Absolutely, yes.&#8221;

Eli&nbsp;

There&#8217;s something really special about a very young artist with a massive platform who&#8217;s actually standing for some real, real important change. F&#8212; capitalism, sorry.

Tetris Kelly&nbsp;&nbsp;

We&#8217;re taking you to the first-ever Daisy Chain Fields in Billboard All Access. We hopped in a car with Lego Group to head to Irvine, California. And once we arrived at the fest, we kicked the day off with the beautiful and talented Eli.

Fan&nbsp;

I was just saying, you&#8217;re beautiful, you&#8217;re amazing. Keep doing what you&#8217;re doing. You&#8217;re super talented. I&#8217;ve been a fan of you for a little bit, but yeah.

I got a phone call on the day that I found out she wanted to have a phone call. I was like, &#8220;What is happening?&#8221; I had no idea she knew my music. I&#8217;m like, &#8220;Maybe Conan Gray showed her, like maybe one of the gays,&#8221; like I don&#8217;t know. I&#8217;m like, &#8220;Who did it?&#8221; I was very moved by the mission statements that she had. I was very moved by the heart to unite women and not tear women down. The unethical and abhorrent inhumane nature of a world with billionaires possessing more than half the wealth of the entire world, while roughly 2 to 3 billion human beings on Earth live without all of their basic human needs met. It was important to me because opportunities like this are very rare. It is such a moving dream to be able to sing on the stage, and like that&#8217;s for like my heart, and that&#8217;s for like me and my personal development. But then like to know that if you&#8217;re gonna even be in front of anyone, there&#8217;s like a responsibility, I feel.

